{"type":"message","id":"562877fb","parentId":"50fc83e8","timestamp":"2026-05-19T03:47:40.866Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The POST /send endpoint is returning Cloudflare error 1101 (Worker exception). This might mean the worker has a bug, or the endpoint expects different data. \n\nLooking at the history API, it uses `threadId` as a query parameter and `X-API-Key` header. The send endpoint might need different field names.\n\nLet me try with `threadId` in the body and other variations.\n\nWait - error 1101 from Cloudflare Workers typically means \"Worker threw an unhandled exception.\" This is a server-side issue with the worker's code, not our request format. The history endpoint works fine but /send throws 1101.\n\n\nI should check if the history endpoint supports a `limit` parameter to see the most recent messages and confirm whether POST /send has a different field name requirement or if there's something else about how the worker expects the request formatted. The 1101 error indicates the worker itself is throwing an exception rather than rejecting our request format—that's a server-side bug I can't fix from here. I've successfully called the history endpoint, but the send endpoint consistently fails with this error, suggesting the platform's /send implementation has an unhandled exception. Let me try one more variation to be sure, but this looks like an infrastructure issue.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-7e929b4b-18d3-43e5-9af0-bd5a2370693c","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try different field names for the send endpoint\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"message\":\"**[Heartbeat 03:45 UTC]**\"}' 2>&1"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model"